    "slug": "palindrome-partitioning",
    "group": "101-200",
    "title": "Palindrome Partitioning",
    "workload": "four 16-character case strings built once, then 150 punches of the full backtracking enumeration. String shape IS the workload: an all-'a' string of length n has 2^(n-1) palindromic partitionings, so the search is exponential in n and two characters change the runtime fourfold. The set mixes all-'a' (maximum branching, every substring is a palindrome), alternating abab (moderate), a no-repeat string (minimum, only single characters) and a structured aabaac pattern, so no single extreme of the search tree dominates. NOTE: the kata's substring is O(n) -- it walks the characters and filters rather than slicing -- and every mirror reproduces that per-piece cost rather than using a native O(1) slice, which would make C/Rust/Go a different algorithm.",
